fltheme -- Themes, the one place to adjust the look
===================================================

One window for everything about how the desktop looks. Each control writes ~/.config/freelfs/desktop.conf and
the running desktop follows at once (libflui apps and the panel watch the file, flcomp reads it for its own
colours, the X window frames, the animations and the panel's edge), so there is no Apply button: the
miniature at the top of every page is drawn from the same values, the real windows are the preview.

Pages (sidebar, like Settings)
  Presets      FreeLFS Dark (the default), FreeLFS Light, Compact, Large; "My presets": save the current look
               under a name, apply or delete saved ones; Reset (every themed key back to the default)
  Colours      scheme dark or light; accent (the six swatches, or six hex digits); a button to the wallpaper
               in Settings > Display
  Fonts        UI font family (IBM Plex Sans, IBM Plex Mono, DejaVu Sans, DejaVu Sans Mono: those that
               are installed), text size 11 to 16 px (13 is the design size)
  Windows      buttons at the right or the left, title bar normal (34 px) or compact (28 px). Corners: square,
               fixed. There is no radius setting and there will not be one.
  Panel        bottom or top edge, height 36 to 60 px, icon size 16 to 28 px
  Animations   on, reduced (fades only) or off; speed 0.5x to 2x

desktop.conf keys (defaults in brackets; a key equal to its default is removed, not written)
  theme=dark|light  accent=green|teal|blue|amber|orange|rose|RRGGBB  font=FAMILY (IBM Plex Sans)
  font_size=10..18 (13)  buttons=right|left  titlebar=normal|compact  panel_position=bottom|top
  panel_height=36..64 (44)  panel_icon_size=16..28 (20)  animations=on|reduced|off  animation_speed=0.1..4 (1.0)
Who reads them: libflui (fl_lk in flui.h, every app; fonts and title bars change live), flcomp (config.c,
theme.c: colours of the indicator, Alt-Tab, overview, lock screen, X frames; panel edge; animations), flpanel
(height, icon size, hairline side). The accent is the same key as Settings > General and the same code:
fl_accents and fl_conf_set of libflui.

Colours are defined once, in libflui's flpalette.h (the compositor includes the same file). `make check`
prints the WCAG contrast of every pair that matters in both schemes and every accent (light: text 15:1,
dim 6.8:1, accents 4.8:1 and better on the panel; dark keeps the tokens it always had).

My presets are small files in ~/.config/freelfs/themes/NAME.theme (next to desktop.conf), key=value lines for
the keys above and nothing else: a theme file cannot set wallpaper= or any other key, unknown lines are
ignored and a file with none of the keys is refused. Names: letters, digits, space, - and _ (32 at most).

Flatpak and GTK apps: every change rewrites two lines in ~/.config/gtk-3.0/settings.ini and gtk-4.0/settings.ini
(gtk-application-prefer-dark-theme, gtk-font-name; other lines are kept; Flatpak shows both read-only to apps).
The portal half is flportal's: its Settings portal answers org.freedesktop.appearance color-scheme and
accent-color from desktop.conf and emits SettingChanged. Qt is not covered.

Command line
  fltheme [--page presets|colours|fonts|windows|panel|animations]
  fltheme --hints | --list | --reset | --apply NAME | --save NAME

Build: make [FLUI=../flui]; make check (contrast, presets, theme files and the hints, no compositor needed);
make install DESTDIR=. Needs libflui. Test hooks: FLUI_PPM=FILE renders a page without a compositor,
FLTHEME_SIZE=WxH, FLTHEME_TEST_SAVE=text; tests/shot.sh PAGE OUT.png [KEY=VALUE...] does it with a scratch HOME.
